ADAPTIVE ROUTING
EVOLAG must continuously monitor the active route.
Example:
Initial route:
Player → Relay A → Fortnite
If Relay A becomes congested:
Player → Relay B → Relay C → Fortnite
The system should automatically evaluate alternatives.
Route switching must use hysteresis and minimum thresholds to prevent constant route switching.
Do not switch simply because another route is 1–2 ms faster.
Only switch when the expected improvement is meaningful and stable.

MULTI-HOP ROUTING
Support intelligent multi-hop routing when it produces a measurable improvement.
Example:
Player → New York → Chicago → Fortnite
instead of:
Player → ISP → Fortnite
The system should automatically determine whether:
Single-hop is better
Two-hop is better
Multi-hop is worse
Never add additional hops solely for complexity.

